## 2026-09-29 implementation addendum from DETRAN R-0020

The local renderer has been used for sealed historical rounds, including a corrective PC chain for R-0018: PC-0020 supersedes PC-0015 while both source PCs remain immutable. The upstream command should make the canonical index a deterministic projection of record/proofs/compliance/closures/PC-*.json, not of free-form record.md text.

Suggested acceptance fixture:
- two rounds with ordinary PCs; one round with PC-0015 -> PC-0020 supersession; each row includes PC id, round id, supersedes (or dash) and merged_as (or dash);
- numeric PC ordering and stable UTF-8/newline/Markdown escaping so repeated render has identical bytes;
- exactly one terminal PC per round, while retaining all historical rows for an append-only correction;
- --check compares the expected bytes to record/derived/indexes/rounds.md without writing; --write emits the canonical bytes and a following --check passes;
- round seal accepts the generated index and refuses a stale one.

Negative fixtures: filename/id mismatch, duplicate PC id, missing superseded PC, cross-round supersession, cycle, two terminal heads, malformed round id, missing closure directory and stale index. Symlink or path escape should not read outside the repository. A failed check/write must not leave a partly rewritten canonical index.

Reference adopter implementation: https://github.com/aarusso-nyx/detran/blob/orchestra/devai-sensors/tools/devai/render-rounds-index.mjs . The local tool is an approved workaround (OD-R20-002=B); migration upstream should preserve index semantics and historical PCs. This gap does not currently block CTG-0004 because the adopter gate is already active.
